Subject: wasix: report the file type of every socket
Last-Update: 2026-09-30

fd_fdstat_get named the type of a socket from its state, and only a
connected TCP stream, a raw socket and a socket not yet bound had one: a
bound or listening TCP socket and a UDP socket reported an unknown type,
and so did each end of a sock_pair pair, which is a duplex pipe.
fd_filestat_get reported the type in the socket inode's stat, which
sock_open and sock_accept leave at the default, unknown. wasix-libc's
getsockopt(SO_TYPE) therefore refused a listener as not a socket, as Go's
net.FileListener on its wasip1 port does, and fstat reported no socket
in any state.

InodeSocket::filetype gives the type a socket's kind implies: a listener
is a stream socket and a UDP socket a datagram socket, as WASI defines
the types, and a socket not yet bound, a bound TCP socket and one
restored from a journal have the type they were created with. Both calls
report it, and fd_fdstat_get reports a sock_pair end as the stream socket
its stat already names.

